WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.299
This is the OCS cable we plugged into the TPU
rack.

2
00:00:07.049 --> 00:00:10.974
Now we follow it to the other end: the SPOCS
rack.

3
00:00:12.324 --> 00:00:20.026
We will look inside a SPOCS rack, at the OCS
shelf and its ports, which leg goes to which

4
00:00:20.026 --> 00:00:26.949
slot, the X and X plus one rule, a worked
example, and how to pull and dress the

5
00:00:26.949 --> 00:00:27.641
bundles.

6
00:00:31.791 --> 00:00:36.890
A SPOCS rack holds four OCS shelves, one in
each slot.

7
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.264
Only these four shelves are yours.

8
00:00:41.614 --> 00:00:44.238
The slots count from the top down.

9
00:00:44.988 --> 00:00:47.207
Slot one is the top shelf.

10
00:00:48.557 --> 00:00:51.117
And slot four is the bottom shelf.

11
00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:57.928
The power, TROSS, rectifier and battery
shelves are pre-installed.

12
00:00:58.678 --> 00:01:00.257
They are not yours.

13
00:01:04.407 --> 00:01:08.055
Each shelf has three hundred twenty LC ports.

14
00:01:08.805 --> 00:01:14.479
They are numbered with three digits, from zero
zero one to three twenty.

15
00:01:15.879 --> 00:01:23.154
Each box on this drawing is a pair of ports:
the odd port on top, the even port below.

16
00:01:23.904 --> 00:01:27.808
Like zero zero one and zero zero two.

17
00:01:29.158 --> 00:01:35.494
The numbers count down a column of twenty,
then move to the next column to the right.

18
00:01:36.844 --> 00:01:42.689
Ports one forty-five to one sixty, shown in
grey, are not used.

19
00:01:44.039 --> 00:01:51.122
The left half, ports one to one sixty, is for
TPU racks one to seventy-two.

20
00:01:51.872 --> 00:01:59.323
The right half, one sixty-one to three twenty,
is for TPU racks seventy-three to one

21
00:01:59.323 --> 00:02:00.299
forty-four.

22
00:02:04.449 --> 00:02:10.017
Here is one OCS bundle arriving at a SPOCS
rack from above.

23
00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:13.412
The legs come in four different lengths.

24
00:02:14.812 --> 00:02:21.768
Legs one and two, blue and orange, are the
shortest: fourteen hundred eighty millimeters,

25
00:02:21.768 --> 00:02:23.879
about four feet ten inches.

26
00:02:24.629 --> 00:02:27.338
They go to slot one, the top shelf.

27
00:02:28.688 --> 00:02:34.576
Legs three and four, green and brown, are
eighteen hundred forty millimeters.

28
00:02:35.326 --> 00:02:36.627
Slot two.

29
00:02:37.977 --> 00:02:43.396
Legs five and six, slate and white, are
twenty-two hundred millimeters.

30
00:02:44.146 --> 00:02:45.511
Slot three.

31
00:02:46.861 --> 00:02:53.688
And legs seven and eight, red and black, are
the longest: twenty-five sixty millimeters.

32
00:02:54.438 --> 00:02:56.678
Slot four, the bottom shelf.

33
00:02:58.028 --> 00:03:02.060
The lengths are built so each pair just
reaches its shelf.

34
00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:09.445
If a leg seems far too short or too long for
its slot, it is probably the wrong leg.

35
00:03:13.595 --> 00:03:15.749
Now, which port on each shelf?

36
00:03:16.499 --> 00:03:20.254
The cutsheet gives your TPU rack a port
number.

37
00:03:21.004 --> 00:03:22.860
The guide calls it X.

38
00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:30.169
Each slot gets two legs: one on port X, and
one on port X plus one.

39
00:03:30.919 --> 00:03:33.501
The odd-numbered leg goes on X.

40
00:03:34.851 --> 00:03:39.053
So legs one, three, five and seven go on port
X.

41
00:03:39.803 --> 00:03:44.283
Legs two, four, six and eight go on port X
plus one.

42
00:03:45.633 --> 00:03:48.215
And here is the part people forget.

43
00:03:48.965 --> 00:03:55.983
Your TPU rack uses the same X on every slot,
and on all three SPOCS racks.

44
00:03:57.333 --> 00:04:03.384
The guide checked this pattern on all eight
thousand six hundred forty bundles in the

45
00:04:03.384 --> 00:04:04.736
reference cutsheet.

46
00:04:08.886 --> 00:04:16.524
The guide's own drawing uses ports zero
seventeen and zero eighteen as its example, so

47
00:04:16.524 --> 00:04:17.590
we will too.

48
00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:21.071
Your real X comes from the cutsheet.

49
00:04:22.421 --> 00:04:27.221
Leg one, blue, goes to slot one, port zero
seventeen.

50
00:04:27.971 --> 00:04:32.835
Leg two, orange, goes to slot one, port zero
eighteen.

51
00:04:34.185 --> 00:04:41.873
Leg three goes to slot two, port zero
seventeen, and leg four to slot two, port zero

52
00:04:41.873 --> 00:04:42.697
eighteen.

53
00:04:43.447 --> 00:04:46.604
The same two ports, one shelf lower.

54
00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:53.821
Then legs five and six on slot three, and legs
seven and eight on slot four.

55
00:04:54.571 --> 00:04:58.261
Always zero seventeen and zero eighteen.

56
00:04:59.611 --> 00:05:06.838
Then you do exactly the same with the orange
cable at SPOCS rack two, and the yellow cable

57
00:05:06.838 --> 00:05:08.443
at SPOCS rack three.

58
00:05:09.793 --> 00:05:17.984
Port zero seventeen is in the left half, so
this TPU rack is in TPU one to seventy-two,

59
00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:21.185
and its bundles dress on the left.

60
00:05:25.335 --> 00:05:27.810
Finally, pulling and dressing.

61
00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:35.259
Pull the OCS bundles starting at the OCS rack,
toward the TPU rack.

62
00:05:36.459 --> 00:05:43.959
The split point, where the bundle breaks into
legs, sits twelve to eighteen inches above the

63
00:05:43.959 --> 00:05:45.589
top of the OCS rack.

64
00:05:46.939 --> 00:05:54.552
Bundles from TPU racks one to seventy-two
leave the tray on the left side of the OCS

65
00:05:54.552 --> 00:05:57.542
rack and are dressed on the left.

66
00:05:58.292 --> 00:06:02.196
Seventy-three to one forty-four go on the
right.

67
00:06:03.546 --> 00:06:06.853
OCS cables run in the tier one tray.

68
00:06:07.603 --> 00:06:14.807
Secure them to the tray only at corners and
exits, three times each, and use waterfalls

69
00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:18.781
centered over the rack's vertical cable
manager.

70
00:06:19.531 --> 00:06:24.545
Bundle with half-inch Velcro every twelve to
eighteen inches.

71
00:06:25.295 --> 00:06:30.265
That is DRS 01.00.03.

72
00:06:31.015 --> 00:06:33.063
Zip ties are not allowed.

73
00:06:34.413 --> 00:06:39.939
Store OCS slack on top of the TPU rack, never
in the tray.

74
00:06:40.689 --> 00:06:46.214
Label and coil the spare legs, or handle them
as your site decided.

75
00:06:47.564 --> 00:06:54.903
And label it all: a wrap-around label on the
bundle near each end, and a flag label on

76
00:06:54.903 --> 00:06:55.756
every leg.

77
00:06:59.906 --> 00:07:07.377
In lesson eleven of the course, practice
matching legs to slots and ports, and deciding

78
00:07:07.377 --> 00:07:10.039
which side a bundle dresses on.

